// REJECTS: Test data within a DataSpace must be created as a DataElementReference type, not an EmbeddedData type.
//
// `testData:` given an inline `ExternalFormat #{...}#` instead of `Reference #{...}#`. The
// grammar rule is `DATA_SPACE_TEST_DATA COLON embeddedData SEMI_COLON`, i.e. it accepts the
// FULL embedded-data island -- every kind any extension registers. The narrowing to exactly
// one kind happens in DataSpaceParseTreeWalker:235, after the island has already parsed.
//
// So a rewrite that wires `embeddedData` here, which is what the .g4 literally says, gets a
// parser that accepts ExternalFormat, Relational, ServiceStore and the rest. The island in
// this fixture is well-formed and parses fine on its own (it is the same shape used in
// ../fixtures/t2-hostedservice.pure); the rejection is entirely the walker's type check.
###DataSpace
DataSpace fixture::neg::InlineTestData
{
  executionContexts:
  [
    {
      name: 'Context 1';
      mapping: fixture::neg::Mapping;
      defaultRuntime: fixture::neg::Runtime;
      testData:
        ExternalFormat
        #{
          contentType: 'application/json';
          data: '[]';
        }#;
    }
  ];
  defaultExecutionContext: 'Context 1';
}
